# TLS termination for the LFCP WebSocket endpoint (WIRE-01 §16: wss://
# except on loopback). Caddy proxies WebSocket upgrades, including the
# lfcp-1 subprotocol header, unchanged.
#
# LFCP_SITE: the host name clients use (default localhost).
# LFCP_TLS:
#   internal          development: certificates from Caddy's own local CA
#                     (trust /data/caddy/pki/authorities/local/root.crt);
#   you@example.org   production: a publicly trusted certificate from
#                     Let's Encrypt (ACME) for LFCP_SITE, which must resolve
#                     here with ports 80 and 443 reachable;
#   /certs/fullchain.pem /certs/privkey.pem
#                     production with your own certificate (mount /certs).
#
# Client address (POST-003): the server applies its per-IP limits to the
# address in X-Forwarded-For, believed only from this proxy (server.toml
# trusted_proxies, the proxy's fixed address in compose.yaml). header_up
# replaces whatever X-Forwarded-For the client sent with one address:
# {client_ip}, the TCP peer. Behind another proxy such as Cloudflare, set
# Caddy's global trusted_proxies and client_ip_headers (e.g.
# CF-Connecting-IP) so {client_ip} is the real client; see README "Docker".
{$LFCP_SITE:localhost} {
	tls {$LFCP_TLS:internal}
	reverse_proxy lfcp-server:7820 {
		header_up X-Forwarded-For {client_ip}
	}
}
